    <details class="help-item">
        <summary>@Strings.Help.DormantQuarantineMeanQ</summary>
        <p>@((MarkupString)Strings.Help.DormantQuarantineMeanA1)</p>
    </details>

    <details class="help-item">
        <summary>@Strings.Help.LogWateringFeedingQ</summary>
        <p>@((MarkupString)Strings.Help.LogWateringFeedingA1)</p>
    </details>

    <details class="help-item">
        <summary>@Strings.Help.LoggedCareWrongFixQ</summary>
        <p>@((MarkupString)Strings.Help.LoggedCareWrongFixA1)</p>
    </details>

    <details class="help-item" id="own-kinds-of-care">
        <summary>Can I log care the app doesn't list?</summary>
        <p>
            Yes. In the care sheet, open <em>What you did</em> and pick <em>Add your own…</em> at the end, or go to
            <em>Settings</em>, then <em>Kinds of care</em>. Give it a name, like misted, bottom watered or refilled the
            humidifier. Your own kinds show under <em>Your own</em> in the list, on one plant and on several at once.
            <em>Counts as</em> says what it is: a <em>Watering</em> counts as water, so a bottom watering is something the
            watering reminder learns from and shows as last watered, and a <em>Feed</em> can have products, water and an
            EC or pH reading. <em>Neither</em> only goes in the care log. <em>Put it on the plant's history</em> also
            writes a line for it on the plant's page, which suits things you don't do often, like wiring a branch.
            In <em>Kinds of care</em> you can rename a kind, change what it counts as and remove it. Entries already
            logged keep the name they had, and changing what a kind counts as only affects new entries unless you
            choose to change the old ones too.
        </p>
    </details>

    <details class="help-item" id="care-intervals">
        <summary>Can the app remind me to feed or repot?</summary>
        <p>
            Yes, with a care interval. Go to <em>Settings</em>, then <em>Care intervals</em>, or tap <em>Set care to come back</em> in
            a plant's Care. Pick what it is, like fertilise, repot, prune or a kind of your own, and how often: every so many days,
            weeks, months or years. <em>Only part of the year</em> limits it, like April to October, or October to March over the new
            year. Then say who it covers: picked plants, a room, a tag like the one on your semi-hydro plants, or all of them. A room
            or a tag follows the plants, so one that is moved or tagged later is covered from then on.
        </p>
        <p>
            Today then has a <em>Care</em> section with what is due, grouped by what to do. Tap the tick to log one plant, or
            <em>Done for all</em> to log the whole group, and <em>Undo</em> takes it back. The put-off button hides one for a day,
            3 days or a week. Each plant is due one interval after the last time you logged it. A plant with nothing logged yet first comes up one interval after you set the interval, so a new one is quiet at first. A plant whose last entry is already longer ago than the interval comes up straight away.
            Feeding stops while a plant is dormant and picks up when it wakes. If you have set round days, care comes up on the round day before it is due.
        </p>
        <p>
            Watering is never on an interval. The watering reminder learns how often each plant needs water from the waterings you log,
            and a fixed schedule would water a plant that isn't ready.
        </p>
    </details>

